            "review_title": "Review at Vegan Pho Nhu Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jago L\n9 contributions\n0\nOne of the best pho’s I have ever had & vegan!\nDec 2019 • Couples\nI travelled to Vietnam 9 years ago and fell in love with the pho dish, I think I had one every day for a month. Now I have returned as a vegetarian & straight away on the trip began searching for vege/vegan pho’s. I did not believe such a thing could exist as the broth especially is prepared and cooked for a huge amount of time using bones from the meat. I tried many different dishes vege restaurants offered, most called vegetarian noodle soup. They were nice but didn’t resemble the pho enough for me to be satisfied such a thing existed until I read the reviews and saw the name of this restaurant. Excitedly visiting this place I was not let down at all! Me and my girlfriend ordered two pho’s which they called pho and not just soup and received two bowls of pho, as a substitute for meat you have some sort of soy bean mix and mushrooms but the broth includes spring onions and all the condiments of pho & the noddles are the same style. The broth is NEXT LEVEL, the whole dish tastes just like an amazing pho and the soy stuff feels a bit like meat but regardless just one of the best tasting pho’s I’ve ever had and no meat! Incredible, had restored my faith that this dish can be made well without meat. If you like pho then come here if you are a vegetarian or not. Atmosphere real great, lots of locals, real local gig with plastic chairs and metal tables, old lady who had set it up 35 years ago Apparantly was lovely and whole meal super cheap 75,000 for two pho’s and some lovely wontons. I want to come back and try more as many more dishes served here.\nRead more\nWritten December 9, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
