            "review_text": "Sam Neu\nBrooklyn, New York11 contributions\n0\nsolid, flavorful, filled with locals, all vegetarian\nJul 2018 • Couples\nSearching for vegan Vietnamese food can often mean eating at Westernized cafes and/or being inundated with fake meat products. I can happily say this spot is neither of these. It's a small place, shared seating, no menus, and great food. We appeared to be the only tourists there when we went for lunch and ordered pho (Pho Chay). Since the place is all vegetarian, we could as easily have pointed to what someone else was eating and just asked for that - there were certainly other varieties to try. An English-speaking staff member served us and helped us settle the bill. Pho-wise, it was delicious: piping hot deeply savory broth, a few mushrooms and other vegetables, tender noodles, mountains of fresh herbs and chiles on the side. No other place we tried veg pho compared to this one. \n\nJust a note: i believe this place is called \"Pho Chay Nu\" as opposed to how it's titled here. The address is correct.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten August 4, 2018",
