            "review_text": "redleaderscotland\nEdinburgh, United Kingdom49 contributions\n0\nBrilliant vegan food\nDec 2017 • Family\nI loved this place - a proper Vietnamese working kitchen that serves up incredible food. We took our 3 young kids in and we asked for some fried rice, some noodles and some pho (no menus) and that's what we got. It was so nice to know that we could eat anything without fear of animal products. The kids were adventurous and tried the dumplings we were given and loved them. Portions are huge and the whole meal about about £10 for the 5 of us. Fresh and tasty with cheap prices and good Viet home cooking. Granny even hangs out on a hammock just at the back of the kitchen!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 28, 2017",
