            "review_text": "matt2lee\nBoston, Massachusetts525 contributions\n0\nBest Pho Ever\nDec 2017 • Friends\nMy friend that I was traveling with is a vegetarian and while in Vietnam, he had to try his first bowl of pho. We wanted to go to Pho Pasteur but unfortunately the broth there all had meat, even the vegetarian one. However the owner kindly told us to try this place, about a 10 minute walk from here. So we decided to give it a try.\nOkay finding this place was difficult as it was down in an alley and it looked like it was in someone’s house. Literally the restaurant was in someone’s garage. Nobody spoke English except one young waitress and she informed us that everything was vegan/vegetarian. As a meat eater I had the vegetarian pho. Wow, all I can say is that the broth was so rich and flavorful it was the best pho I’ve ever had. My friend that had the pho really enjoyed it too. \nThe only unfortunate thing was that everybody spoke Vietnamese (we were at a hole in the wall place so what could we expect...). One of the older ladies showed us how much two bowls of pho was so thinking it was 50 dong each, she gave us 20 back so total of two bowls of pho was 80. I have to say that she was very honest and didn’t rip off two tourists so I must commend her and this place for catering to two Americans who were just trying to find a bowl of pho before heading out the next day.\nAll I can say is that if you are a veg and want pho in Saigon, this is the place!!!\nRead more\nWritten December 26, 2017",
