            "review_text": "MDG\nNorth Shields, United Kingdom119 contributions\n0\nGreat Pho\nFeb 2017 • Couples\nThis establishment was recommended by our hotel as being good for vegetarians so we were in the area so decided to call in.\n\nThe restaurant is open fronted onto the quiet street with the dining area being raised up to a higher level than the road. There is only seating for about 20 people.\n\nWhen we entered we were warmly greeted by a member of staff/chef/waitress in Vietnamese. There are no menus other than those listed on the wall and all the dishes are in the local language. The lady that greeted us said that they were famous for their Pho meals so we decided to have what ever she recommended as we couldn't understand what else was on offer on the wall menu.\n\nThe food was delicious with a huge bowl of soup with tasty noodles and plenty of vegetables mixed in. Worth the effort in walking here for lunch. Whilst sitting at our table we were able to watch all the women working in the kitchen area as it is part of the restaurant to the side of where people eat. As we watched it was good to see that particular attention was paid to cleanliness with the cooks continually washing there hands. Overall a tasty meal at a good price.\n\nHad this restaurant not been recommended we would ordinarily have walked past but is well worth a visit for tasty food and freiendly staff\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 26, 2017",
